Z||000007||skitime||05-20-2001||09:32 PM||||We had a great weekend at the show.  I wish you all could of been there. Meet a lot of great people with beautiful cars.  I was also pleased to have many compliments on my car which helps make all the hard work worthwhile.  Of course there is more work to do.  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P5190028.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P5190039.jpg">  <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 05-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Old Lar||05-20-2001||10:42 PM||||For those who want big wheels: Pisa Corps Jalapeno with 20" wheels.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Jalapeno_1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Y&B.jpg"> <P>Old Lars with his Mod GT .  Didn't stand a chance with the Norstars, turbos and supercharged cars there. It looks like it is stock, but it'snot.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/OldLars.jpg"> <P>I still have more two rolls of 35mm went in today + CD processing.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||kslish||05-21-2001||12:24 AM||||My pics should be in sometime Tuesday.  <P>This year's Carlisle show was the best that I have been to over the past three years I've been going to this show.  I had a great time talking to everyone (the day flew by so quick, I was scrambling to take pictures at the end of the show).  It was nice seeing some familiar faces and meeting some new ones as well.  The weather was great (although I got a little sunburnt...gotta remember the sunscreen next time).  <P>For anyone that I didn't meet face to face at the show, I was the guy that cleaned up at the raffle winning the KYB suspension and the PISA tailight certificate.  First time that I have won anything at a raffle!<P>I was happy to see Lisa and Chris (northstar87) win, since I caravaned out to Carlisle with them (although my Iron Duke got a little overworked cruising at about 75mph following them on the Turnpike, the exhaust heat got to the starter causing it to refuse to restart at a fuel stop for about 15 minutes).  Chris's Northstar has the meanest exhaust sound this side of a Nascar stocker when he gets on it.  And my GT now has a decent pair of tan sunvisors thanks to Lisa.<P>Hope a lot of you show up again at the GM Nationals in Carlisle at the end of June (I'm already making plans) or at one of the other major Fiero shows this year.  I'm going to try to make it to as many as I can.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR> <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||84Bill||05-21-2001||01:34 AM||||Met up with some of the folks here<BR>Skitime<BR>Veronica GT<BR>Fleabitdog<BR>Fierodave2001<BR>FieroLisa<BR>Old Lar<BR>Northstar<BR>Jaguiler<P>and a few others I was the guy wearing the Black Comcast hat and blue shades<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-21-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000011||84Bill||05-21-2001||01:39 AM||||I have some pics and comments up on my page stop by and check them out!<BR> <A HREF="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/theshows.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/theshows.htm</A><P>I had no problem with my 2.5 overheating   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Shows/carlisle/image002.jpg">  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula||05-21-2001||08:42 AM||||did anyone take pics of the red SE (looks lke a formula) beside phil's formula.  I loved the way he made the parking lights opening bigger and put driving lights in it (future mod for mine now).<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigformulagt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Black88GT||05-21-2001||10:30 AM||||I took a bunch of pics of that red SE.  That was Earl Sessions Fiero.  It was sooo sweet.  I am giving all my pics to Wudman the guy who does the Fiero photo-rama at <A HREF="http://www.thisisfun.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thisisfun.com</A>  so he can post them for all to see.  I used my good old non-digital camera so thats why there's a delay.||||reg||1
Z||000014||TheFiero64||05-21-2001||10:36 AM||||Here is my first post since being back, It was awsome <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. The weather was great exept for the sunburn on me and Jaygee79. There were a lot of sweet cars and I was overwelmed by the size. I am upset that I didn't even get the chance to meet everyone. I also lost some time working in the MAFOA tent. I am also happy that I got <B>1st place in my class</B> High millage notchback. I almost went into custom notchback but didn't have time to put my new painted valve cover on, so I desided that it would be better for me to enter high milage. I guess it worked <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. I have some pics that I let jaygee take but, it seems that the camara was on the incorrect setting and they all are a little blury  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I will try to post the better ones when I look through them. I can't wait for the next show. It was a great time. Congrats to all who went. All the cars were sweet and deserved a prize.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000015||Raydar||05-21-2001||10:38 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>Thanks guys, the class I was in was Custom Fastback... I'm so proud of my car   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Doesn't that make you feel a bit vindicated after that previous episode where you weren't even allowed to compete, after they took your registration fee?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||14
Z||000016||FieroLisa||05-21-2001||12:00 PM||||Yah, but I essentially paid $50 for that stinkin trophy!!! Its OK though, this year was a lot more fun because 1) I wasn't pi$$ed (until the end of the day when I got a *little* mad at someone  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) and 2) the sun was shining and I was able to work on my car show farmers tan!||||reg||1
