Z||000018||84Bill||05-21-2001||12:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>So... where's the PFF-members group photo?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>You know I was wondering about that myself. I think we need to appoint someone to the task at the next show right after the awards.<BR>I had my PFF window sign but the shirt wouldn't come out right (3 tries) so I shelfed it for now. It will be ready for the next show  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000019||northstar87||05-21-2001||12:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B> Its OK though, this year was a lot more fun because 1) I wasn't pi$$ed (until the end of the day when I got a *little* mad at someone   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) and 2) the sun was shining and I was able to work on my car show farmers tan!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Lisa,<BR>   Looks like you have alot of fans!  Hey what about spending time with me and the Gilbert family? Ha! I had a blast this weekend.  Thanks again to the Gilberts for putting up with Lisa and I.  I really enjoyed meeting many people on the list. I will see everybody at the Dells!<P>Chris Moore<BR>1986 GT Convertible Northstar<BR>1987 GT Northstar (approx. driven 1300 miles this weekend) 26 MPG  A new record!!<BR>1988 GT T-TOP 3.4 5 speed<BR>1988 GT T-TOP Stock||||reg||1
Z||000020||Fiero5||05-21-2001||02:41 PM||||As many on here know, I was planning on going right up till the very last minute the day before (Thursday night). Then I discovered that my Dad needed my help at the last minute, and added to that I couldn't get my Friday paycheck a day earlier. I could have borrowed the money for the weekend, but when my Dad says help - I'm there!<P>I see the weather was nice. I went last year and it rained almost the whole morning and was chilly and yucky the rest of the day. <BR>The good news is that there is always next year. <P>My Dad decided to use the nice weekend for repairing part of his roof. Thursday evening he hinted to me that he could realy use some help on Saturday and Sunday, so the money problem was a good excuse to stay home and help him. He has done enough for me a million times over, it was the least I could do for him.<P>This Sunday Marian (Fiero2) and I are having a memorial day Fiero weekend at our place for any Fiero lovers who want to come. We have quite a few already who have committed to coming, and of course with Fieros, the more the merrier.<P>Just let us know if you would like to come, and I can provide directions and so we will be prepared with a count. Last minute arrivals are always welcom however. Marian says she is all set with food, so nobody is "required" to bring anything other than themselves and at least one (1) Fiero each.<P>Hope to see some of you who live near us in New England or maybe in the area for whatever reason at our place on Sunday. <P><BR>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero1sig.JPG">                   <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||6
Z||000021||FieroLisa||05-21-2001||03:14 PM||||Speaking of which, Yah I want to thank the Gilbert's for putting up with me in my constant half-asleep state this weekend. I was not fully awake at any point from Thursday till today! (My eyes are finally fully open now)<P>All in all, a great weekend, one of the best car shows I've been too, not because I won a trophy, but because I got to stay with friends and meet lots of new people from the forum. ||||reg||1
Z||000022||Fierochic88||05-21-2001||03:43 PM||||No sweat guyz!  Come again soon!  What better than to drive to Carlisle in a convoy of 10 Fieros!||||reg||10
Z||000023||Fierodave2001||05-21-2001||05:01 PM||||Thanks for a shot of my car, I still can't believe I brought the camera,<BR>but no film.<P>I guess I'll break down & get one of them their digital thingy things.<P>I also made a shirt to bring, and forgot that to!<P>I'm just glad I brought the keys to drive it off the trailer. - That would<BR>have been sad. ||||reg||1
