Z||000034||Eric_PA||05-21-2001||09:55 PM||||It was a great day at the show. Got slightly burned on the neck and face, but well worth it. I didn't get around as much as I wanted to meet people, but did find that I was in good company there. I had a great time caravaning with four other people from the area.<P>WMEBERT, that car belongs to Chad, I don't think that he gets on here. If you want to get in touch with him it would be best to get in touch with Rockcrawl here on the forum.<P>MoneypitGt.. Didn't see you there... did you get the QUAD swap done?<P>Skitime... definitly liked your custom front end. first class and one of a kind.. nice<P><BR> <p>[This message has been edited by Eric_PA (edited 05-21-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000035||MoneypitGT||05-21-2001||10:34 PM||||Hey Eric, couldn't make it, I ended up having to work, it sucked, I soooo wanted to go. As far as the QUAD goes well it's kind of done, for now anyway. I had changed plans a little. I am doing a T3/T4 turbo and intercooler setup on the Q4, so I have a lot of work to do yet. I am having the engine O ringed and building up the bottom end so it won't fly apart. It will be interesting I must say. <BR> Chris <P>------------------<BR><B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||1
